Expose Arrow result collection through the C API

Adds two functions (see duckdb-arrow-collector-request.md for the upstream
feature request this implements):

  - duckdb_pending_prepared_arrow(stmt, rows_per_batch, &pending): submits the
    prepared statement in the Arrow result format (ArrowFormat), so the
    engine's workers assemble Arrow record batches during execution instead of
    materializing data chunks that a second pass converts.
  - duckdb_result_arrow_array_stream(&result, &stream): moves the collected
    batches out of the executed result into a caller-provided Arrow C stream
    interface ArrowArrayStream.

The format travels with the query's QueryParameters, so the connection is not
reconfigured. The stream copies the schema the format resolved at submission,
so it depends on neither the connection nor the result. The chunk-based
accessors refuse a result in another format (DuckDBResultData::IsOtherFormat):
duckdb_row_count / duckdb_rows_changed return 0, chunk fetches return nothing
without putting the result into an error state, and the deprecated
materialization path refuses it.

C API v2 offers this as duckdb_v2_prepared_statement_execute_arrow. In v1, only
the deprecated duckdb_execute_prepared_arrow uses the Arrow format, and it
cannot be driven task by task.

Note for upstreaming: duckdb.h is generated from api_spec/v1 by capigen
(scripts/capi_v1_regen.sh); this patch edits the generated header directly. An
upstream PR must add YAML definitions (unstable lifecycle, extension API
offsets) and regenerate instead, plus tests.

